Two failures, both of them the reviewer's second finding, produced by a machine instead of by
reading the code. The archive call sat at line 461, after the write at line 459, and its return
value was discarded. The manifest checks pass on both checkouts, because the manifest is a
separate correction.

## Exit codes

    before                                             1
    after                                              0
    manifest with one digest altered on purpose        1

The third run is the control. A checker that cannot fail is not evidence, so the console.log
digest was replaced with zeros in a copy of the manifest, and the script reported that row and
no other.
